<!-- BEGIN_EMBEDDED_FILE path="runtime/EMBEDDED_NOTICE.txt" sha256="cfb09c420c32515ddb73b8304d845febe182c7d4aaef1c793335ace3d274c627" -->
~~~~text
scPURE.skill embedded runtime notice

This runtime is an independently written, behavior-compatible implementation for the scPURE.skill workflow. It does not contain or redistribute source code from the PURE repository and does not download PURE scripts at runtime.

All Python, R, Seurat, R/Bioconductor DESeq2, BEDTools, BLAST+, and pyGenomeTracks components must run inside the single scPURE_agent environment. Scientific execution is blocked when required pinned versions are missing, mismatched, or resolved outside that environment. pyclusterprofiler is an optional same-environment enhancement only when its dependency import smoke test succeeds; otherwise the embedded local GO-BP ORA plus Wang semantic-similarity implementation is used. MapMan/Mercator hierarchy tables are supported through a deterministic local BIN-level ORA, defaulting to BIN level 3.

Canonical gene IDs remain in machine-readable CSV files. Human-facing report tables, plot labels, track titles, and figure annotations use a unique gene symbol whenever available; duplicated symbols are rendered as symbol_geneID and missing symbols fall back to geneID.

Genome tracks use promoter-centered windows, direct and homolog evidence on separate pages, no more than four signal tracks per page by default, compact symbol-first labels, suppressed peak labels, and a dedicated layout audit. Scientific figures are vector PDF with CSV source tables.

The formal English DOCX is a descriptive output report only. It contains no executive summary, biological interpretation, literature synthesis, discussion, recommendations, or scientific conclusions. Tables and figures are capped, absolute input paths are hidden from the main report, and complete artifacts remain in their stage directories.

When no explicit thread count is supplied, the runtime samples currently idle CPUs once, resolves floor(one half of idle available logical CPUs), records the decision, and reuses that count for all multithread-capable stages.
~~~~
