## 26. Embedded validation status

The Python runtime, environment bootstrap, optional pyclusterprofiler runner,
and bundled tests must pass `python -m py_compile`. The 28 bundled tests cover
contrast exclusivity, mandatory cell balancing, sample-pair rules, GO Wang
similarity and ancestor propagation, MapMan BIN parsing, identifier matching and ORA, thread
resolution, transcript/promoter selection, peak-manifest expansion, direct and
homolog validation priority, input hashing, the single-environment contract,
symbol-first duplicate-safe labels, readable separated genome-track layouts,
descriptive-only report generation, PURE-aligned CatBoost defaults, edge-masked fold stability and rank statistics, directional TF ranking and pooled out-of-fold metrics, absolute-path suppression, report/track
manifest blockers, and fixed versioning.

The report smoke test must verify that a known symbol replaces its gene ID in
human-facing output, that absolute input paths do not appear, that no executive
summary or biological-interpretation heading exists, and that
`report_policy.json` records zero conclusion-language lint violations. The track
layout test must verify direct/homolog page separation, no more than four signal
tracks under defaults, compact symbol labels, suppressed peak labels, explicit
plot-width/label-fraction options, and `track_layout_audit.csv`.

Both R scripts must be parsed and smoke-tested through `Rscript` inside
`scPURE_agent`. Bootstrap must create or repair only `scPURE_agent`, run the
complete bundled test suite, write one explicit package lock, and write
`pyclusterprofiler_status.json`. Failure of the optional pyclusterprofiler
dependency smoke test must select the embedded local GO-BP ORA plus Wang
workflow without creating another environment. MapMan enrichment remains
available because it is implemented locally. A successful bootstrap does not
substitute for validating user data.

## 27. Changelog

### 0.3.1 (2026-11-22)

- MapMan ORA now matches annotation identifiers to modeled gene IDs case-insensitively
  and tolerates Mercator protein/transcript suffixes (`_p001`, `.t1`); previously,
  lower-case Mercator identifiers could leave MapMan enrichment empty. New unit test.
- Documented that the `tune: auto` switch is decided from a baseline on all labeled
  genes while hyperparameters are searched only inside outer training folds.
- Manifest template focus TFs set to MYBR29 and MYBR19, matching the example prompts.
- Markdown heading spacing fixed; version strings updated.

### 0.3.0 (2026-11-03)

- PURE provenance: added what PURE is, the PURE Module 1-3 correspondence table and
  the citation (Li et al., 2026, *Plant Commun.* 102118).
- CatBoost defaults aligned with PURE Module 2: 1,000 iterations, learning rate
  0.05, depth 6, l2 3.0, `Balanced` class weights, 5-fold stratified CV with one
  repeat by default.
- Fixed `mean_abs_rank`, which previously ranked filtered zero entries.
- Fixed fold-stability ranks, which previously used unfiltered SHAP; they now use
  edge-filtered SHAP like all other rankings.
- New directional ranking (`SHAP_directional_TF_ranking.csv`,
  `top_TFs_directional_SHAP.pdf`) giving net signed edge-filtered SHAP toward the
  focal and reference classes.
- ROC/PR plots now show the pooled out-of-fold curve with AUC/AP
  (`pooled_out_of_fold_metrics.json`) over light per-fold curves; the performance
  plot shows fold-level points.
- Journal-ready plotting theme (7-pt Arial, 0.6-pt axes, single-column figure sizes);
  binding-evidence markers are drawn as real star/diamond markers instead of glyphs
  missing from Arial.
- Report: key figures prioritized and inserted at readable size; booktabs-style
  tables with shaded headers; quiet note style.
- Rewritten example prompts (full English, full Chinese, minimal) and first-response
  checklist.
